<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bases Orgánicas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Organic Bases of the Mexican Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bases Orgánicas were a centralist constitution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, drafted by a junta of notables under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a> and promulgated on 12 June 1843. They replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siete-leyes">Siete Leyes</a> of 1836, kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> under central control and strengthened the presidency. They remained in force until the federal constitution of 1824 was restored in 1846.</p></div>
